drm: h713-afbd: a page flip on the video plane without the ring is the address slots and DIRTY

The keystone warp's frames go on the video plane since 24.09.2026 (NV12, the channel the
firmware's picture controls act on), sixty commits a second. The plane's update ran the
whole enable sequence for every one of them - the size, stride and crop words, the gate,
the mux, then VIDEO_READY and a poll on it until the next vsync - which held the commit
worker for a frame per flip (three kworkers at 5-7 % each on the HY310) and, through the
stall on the previous commit's cleanup, the daemon behind it.

A flip on a plane that is already up without the ring, with the same format, size and
pitch as before, now writes the four address slots and DIRTY under the ring lock and
returns: the latch the ring's vsync notifier uses, taken by the hardware at the next
vsync, the flip completed by the CRTC's vblank event as before. Measured after: the
kworkers under 1.5 %, 59.4 frames a second, the warp's self-check 0 differing rows.
The enable path is unchanged; a ring commit or a geometry change still takes it.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -1166,6 +1166,37 @@
 	nv16 = fb->format->format == DRM_FORMAT_NV16;
 	ring = s->hdmi_ring;
 
+	/*
+	 * A page flip on a plane that is already up without the ring (the
+	 * keystone warp's NV12 frames, 60 a second since 24.09.2026): the four
+	 * address slots and DIRTY, which the hardware takes at the next vsync -
+	 * the same latch the ring's notifier uses. The full sequence below
+	 * re-arms the channel and then polls VIDEO_READY until that vsync,
+	 * which held the commit worker for a frame on every flip (three
+	 * kworkers at 5-7 % each, measured) and, through the stall on the
+	 * previous commit's cleanup, the daemon with it. Geometry and format
+	 * cannot change here: the check refuses a source rectangle other than
+	 * the whole framebuffer, and h713-tv hands out three buffers of one
+	 * size.
+	 */
+	if (h->video_active && !ring && !h->ring_follow) {
+		const struct drm_plane_state *old_state =
+			drm_atomic_get_old_plane_state(state, plane);
+
+		if (old_state && old_state->fb &&
+		    old_state->fb->format->format == fb->format->format &&
+		    old_state->fb->width == fb->width &&
+		    old_state->fb->height == fb->height &&
+		    old_state->fb->pitches[0] == fb->pitches[0]) {
+			y = lower_32_bits(drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(fb, new_state, 0));
+			c = lower_32_bits(drm_fb_dma_get_gem_addr(fb, new_state, 1));
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&h->ring_lock, flags);
+			h713_afbd_queue_pair(h, y, c);
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&h->ring_lock, flags);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/* The hardware mux is exclusive: quiesce RGB before source 0. */
 	if (!h->video_active) {
 		writel((h->rgb_ctrl_active | BIT(31)) & ~BIT(0),
